<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>A Step-by-Step Guide to Implementing Production Management</b></h3>
                <p>A production management solution can help manufacturers plan production, manage work orders, monitor operations, coordinate resources, and improve production visibility through connected digital workflows.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Production Strategy Planning: Identify production planning, scheduling, work order, resource, capacity, and operational requirements.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Centralized Production Information: Organize work orders, production schedules, resources, materials, and operational information in a structured platform.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Production Workflow Automation: Automate work orders, production updates, approvals, alerts, and routine operational activities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Secure Access: Apply role-based access controls so production teams can access information relevant to their responsibilities.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Continuous Production Optimization: Use production data, analytics, and user feedback to improve workflows and operational performance.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>Key Critical Factors for a Successful Production Management Solution</b></h3>
                <p>Production management requires a strong balance of planning, scheduling, resource utilization, data visibility, automation, and user experience.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Clear Production Objectives: Define measurable goals for throughput, utilization, production efficiency, downtime, and delivery performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Accurate Production Data: Maintain current work orders, schedules, materials, resources, and production status information.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Workflow Automation: Automate production notifications, approvals, work-order updates, and routine tasks.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Resource Visibility: Provide clear visibility into machines, labor, materials, capacity, and production schedules.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  User Adoption: Design intuitive production workflows and train teams on the solution.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Production Management" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-center m-3" alt="Production Management" /></div>
            </div>
