<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-4">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 me-3 p-3" alt="Production Management" /></div>
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/woman-tech-desk-chart-bureau.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Production Management" /></div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-8 Imgborder" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Common Production Management Challenges and How to Address Them</b></h3>
                <p>Manufacturers may face production delays, manual planning, limited resource visibility, inconsistent processes, and disconnected production information.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Manual Production Planning: Digitize production planning and scheduling workflows to reduce repetitive work.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Limited Production Visibility: Use centralized dashboards to monitor work orders, production status, capacity, and performance.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Resource Conflicts: Maintain current resource and capacity information to support better scheduling.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Production Delays: Use alerts, workflow tracking, and analytics to identify issues earlier.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Disconnected Operations: Connect production workflows with inventory, procurement, quality, and ERP systems.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>The Importance of Customization in Production Management</b></h3>
                <p>Every manufacturer has different production processes, work-order structures, resources, and scheduling rules. Customization helps the solution reflect actual operations.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Customize Production Workflows: Align work orders and production steps with the organization's manufacturing processes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Create Role-Based Workspaces: Give planners, supervisors, operators, and managers relevant information and actions.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Automate Production Alerts: Configure notifications for delays, approvals, material requirements, and production milestones.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Build Custom Dashboards: Provide production KPIs, capacity, throughput, downtime, and work-order insights.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Gather User Feedback: Continuously refine production processes based on operational feedback.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

