<section>
    <div class="container">
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-lg-8" align="justify">
                <h3><b>Managing Change for Successful Production Management Adoption</b></h3>
                <p>Production teams need practical workflows that fit their daily activities. A structured change approach helps users adopt new digital production processes.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Explain the Production Vision: Show how the solution improves planning, visibility, coordination, and productivity.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Engage Production Teams: Involve planners, supervisors, operators, maintenance, quality, and management stakeholders.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Role-Based Training: Train users on the production functions relevant to their roles.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Roll Out in Phases: Introduce workflows in manageable stages and monitor production adoption.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Provide Ongoing Support: Resolve user questions and continuously improve production workflows.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul><br />

                <h3><b>How to Optimize Production Management for Maximum ROI</b></h3>
                <p>Production management should continuously evolve to improve throughput, resource utilization, visibility, and operational outcomes.</p>
                <ul class="list-unstyled">
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Define Production KPIs: Measure throughput, utilization, downtime, cycle time, schedule adherence, and production efficiency.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Integrate Core Systems: Connect production with inventory, procurement, quality, ERP, and analytics systems.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Improve User Experience: Simplify production screens, work orders, updates, and approvals.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Review Production Performance: Regularly assess schedules, resources, bottlenecks, and operational outcomes.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p><i class="bi bi-check2-circle color"></i>  Leverage Automation and Analytics: Use automation and analytics to identify bottlenecks and improve production decisions.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-lg-4 Imgborder">
                <div><img src="~/assets/img/dynamics365/Developer2.webp" class="img-fluid text-start ms-0 mb-5 mt-3 me-3 p-3" alt="Production Management" /></div>
